of sensors, a defensive perimeter which can find and
zap incoming bugs.  Cargo ships are recieved and inspected for bugs 
at a separate port facility.  A big issue is whether Earth
can build bugs tiny enough to get past the space colony's bugs.
Earth's bugs will be higher tech, but they have a longer
voyage to get out there.  Another issue is how easy it is
to find and track down bugs once they've hidden themselves
in the noisy bowels of the habitat/industrial park constellations.
Operating behind the stealth curtains, bugs either must use 
wide-beam radio or rocket their way back out to transmit info.  
Either might reveal their presence.

